Sums of Zeros for Certain Special Functions   Key words and phrases: q-Airy function (Ramanujan's entire function);
q-Bessel function; Bessel function; Airy function; Riemann zeta function;
Dirichlet L-series.

A recursion equation for prime numbers   It is shown that the first $n$ prime numbers $p_1,...,p_n$ determine the next
one by the recursion equation $$ p_{n+1} =\lim\limits_{s\to +\infty}
[\prod\limits^n_{k=1} (1-\frac{1}{p^s_k}) \sum\limits^\infty_{j=1}
\frac{1}{j^s} -1]^{-1/s}. $$ The upper limit on the sum can be replaced by
$2p_n -1$, and the result still holds.
